course: dictionary
lesson: 9260
title: A word from the steppe
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. This is its context, and it leaves clues. «Sousliks are ground squirrels of the steppe that eat seeds, roots and insects.» Ground squirrels and eating seeds tell you that a souslik is a small animal, not a plant or a bird.
explain: Look for clues about place too. The steppe is a grassy plain, so a souslik lives on wide, open grassland. «The speckled souslik has white dots and is now rare» tells you that sousliks are not all common, and some kinds are in danger.
explain: Always check your meaning. Swap it into the sentence: «Sousliks are a main food for steppe eagles.» If a souslik is a small squirrel, then eagles eat small squirrels, and that makes sense. If the meaning does not fit, look again at the clues.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A souslik is a small ground squirrel that lives in burrows on the grassy plains (steppes) of Eastern Europe and Central Asia, including Ukraine.
fact: «Suslik» is another spelling of souslik, and the word comes from Russian.
fact: Sousliks stand up to watch for eagles, polecats and foxes, and they are a main food for steppe eagles and steppe polecats.
fact: In nature lessons, sousliks show how small animals survive by digging burrows and sleeping through the cold winter (hibernating).
exercise: «Sousliks are ground squirrels of the steppe that eat seeds, roots and insects.» What is a souslik? | A large bird that eats seeds | A type of steppe grass | *A small ground squirrel
exercise: «The speckled souslik has white dots and is now rare.» Find and copy one word that means not common. | speckled | *rare | dots | white
exercise: «Sousliks stand up to watch for eagles, polecats and foxes.» Why do they stand up? | To sing to other sousliks | To eat more seeds | *To watch out for hunters | To dig a bigger burrow
test: «The steppe is a grassy plain where sousliks live.» What does steppe mean? | A rocky mountain | *A grassy plain | A forest of tall trees | A cold lake
test: Where do sousliks live? | In the hot desert of Egypt | *On the grassy plains of Eastern Europe and Central Asia | In tall city trees | In the deep sea
exam: «Sousliks are a main food for steppe eagles, imperial eagles and steppe polecats, so when souslik colonies disappear these hunters disappear too.» What does disappear mean? | Make a loud noise | Come closer to the burrows | *Go away or vanish | Grow bigger and stronger
